{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C2"],
      "pins": ["C2.1", "C2.2"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "GND"],
      "observed": "C2 is specified as 100pF (footprint C_0805_2012Metric) and is the only capacitor on the +5V rail, which is the output of the LM1117-5.0 regulator (U1.2) and the supply for both ATtiny MCUs (U2.8, U3.8).",
      "expected": "A regulator output / MCU decoupling capacitor should be at least ~100nF (typically 10µF for an LM1117, which requires a minimum output capacitance for stability), not 100pF.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"C2\")\n      (value \"100pF\")\n      (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+5V\") (class \"Default\")\n      (node (ref \"C2\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"VO\") (pintype \"power_out\"))"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "C2 +5V 0 100p"}
      ],
      "impact": "The LM1117-5.0 has essentially no output capacitance, which can cause the 5V rail to oscillate/ring, and the ATtiny MCUs have no effective supply decoupling, potentially causing erratic operation or resets.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design is largely consistent, but C2 on the +5V regulator output/MCU supply rail is 100pF, roughly three orders of magnitude too small for an LM1117 output capacitor and for MCU decoupling, which would make the 5V rail unstable."
}

